WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.810
- I don't think in my
life I've turned redder.

00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:05.300
- (bleep) Why.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.360
- This is my worst texting
experience I've ever had.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.670
So when I was in high
school, I was dating this guy

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.260
that I thought I was into,
but then New Years Eve

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.880
was rolling around and we
had planned this whole party

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.890
with my friend who was
also dating his friend

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.130
and it was this whole thing.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:21.500
And I realized like right
before New Years Eve

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.400
that I didn't really like him anymore.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.030
And I was texting my friend
about it and how I was

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.990
planning on breaking up
with him and how annoyed

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.770
with him I was, while I
was sitting next to him.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.970
And I thought I was texting my friend

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.630
but he all of a sudden got
this text and he looked

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.107
at his phone and then he looked at me.

00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:39.200
And I was like, "What?"

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.950
And he was like "What the (bleep)?"

00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:43.540
And I was like, "What? I don't know.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.450
Like, I don't have your phone."

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.280
And he was like, "You
just sent me that text."

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.690
And I was like, "What text?"

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.240
And I started to panic a little bit,

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.950
and I was like, "Oh my God, oh my God."

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.850
So I looked at my phone, and sure enough

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:57.160
I hadn't texted my friend
the 10 page thing about

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.190
how annoyed with him I was,
I had texted it to him.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.540
We still went to the party.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.669
We had fun, but we broke
up a couple days later

00:01:04.669 --> 00:01:06.170
to no one's surprise.

00:01:06.427 --> 00:01:10.787
- So I'm like really bad at
saving numbers in my phone.

00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:13.530
There's a lot of people in
my text messages that just

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:16.080
don't have saved numbers, and I just don't

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.910
always know who's texting me.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.690
So there's this one time
that I had this big crush

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.560
on this guy and he had a 310 number

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.053
or something like that, and
all of a sudden, one day

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:31.270
he asked me to go to his DJ
show up in North Hollywood.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.300
I'm like, "Oh my God,
oh my God, he likes me.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.560
He wants me to go to his DJ show.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.090
Oh my God, oh my God, I should go!"

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.540
Basically, this place is far.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:41.440
This place is so far, and I'm
driving for love, you know?

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:46.074
For potential love, and so I
get there and it's like this

00:01:46.074 --> 00:01:50.000
weird bar, and I'm like,
okay, I'll find him.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.270
So I'm looking around for
him, and then I see this guy

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:59.670
that I know, and basically
he's this creepy guy

00:01:59.745 --> 00:02:03.110
whose number I got a long time
ago and he kept wanting me

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:06.800
to hang out with him, and
he's DJing that night.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.210
And so I'm just like why is he
DJing here? What's going on?

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.910
And then I'm like, (bleep).

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.239
And so I look at my phone and I realize

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:17.030
that he was the one texting me.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.340
Creepy dude was texting
me, not crush dude.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.740
It was actually creepy dude.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.820
And so now, creepy dude thinks that

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.930
I'm so into him that I
would drive all the way

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.800
to his DJ set just to hang out with him.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.840
You know, you'd think I'd
learn from that, but I don't.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.130
- So probably about three or
four years after I graduated

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.460
college, I was working in
New York City, I was having

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.940
a steady job, feeling great about life.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.190
And, you know, Facebook was
the way you communicated

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:50.670
with a lot of people back in college.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.900
And so I went on a limb and
I was talking to this girl.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.050
Like, "Hey, I see you're
in New York City."

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.250
She just graduated about
a year or so before.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.120
I was like, "We should meet up for a drink

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.810
or grab some dinner or something."

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.480
She wrote back, she's like,
"Hey, I would love to.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.330
I actually work in Midtown,"
which is where I work.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.730
Like, "Great let's just go,
grab some dinner after work."

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.960
She was like, "Fantastic."

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.470
I didn't want to think it was a date,

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.400
we didn't call it anything.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.150
It was just like hanging out,
but I was just so excited

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.770
to be hanging one-on-one.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.830
We've always vibed, we've
always had good conversations

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.116
in college, but I was always too afraid

00:03:21.116 --> 00:03:23.820
to ask her out, or I was
always dating someone

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.750
or she was always dating someone.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.750
So just never the opportunity arose.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.160
I told a couple of my friends
I was going out with her.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.960
Some of my friends that went
to college with us as well.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.110
They were texting me throughout the night

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.590
and this is before even iPhones.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.070
This is just like regular
old school Nokia phones,

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.940
you have to press like two three times

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.020
to get to B or C and stuff like that.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.995
And so I'm texting her,
she went to the bathroom.

00:03:46.995 --> 00:03:49.913
I text some friends like,
"Yeah, it's going well.

00:03:49.913 --> 00:03:51.580
We're just having good conversation."

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.350
I'm not stressing about it.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.500
Couple drinks go down, and
so I just pick up my phone,

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.420
I start texting my friends.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.470
I'm like, "I can't believe I'm
hanging out with this girl.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:03.880
She's so (bleep) beautiful.
I hope something happens."

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.140
I can't remember the exact text,

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.330
but I just remember saying
she is so (bleep) beautiful.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.870
And her phone vibrates, and she goes,

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.360
"Sorry, it might be my friend."

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:14.390
She opens up the phone,
and it's a text from me.

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:18.170
I texted her I can't believe
how (bleep) beautiful she is.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.570
Like, I'm so happy to be
on this date right now.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.250
And she looks at me, and she goes, "Huh."

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.110
And I go, "What? Is everything alright?"

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.550
She goes, "Yeah, but
did you mean to text me

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:29.640
how beautiful I was?"

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.150
I don't think in my
life I've turned redder.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:37.150
Like a full shade of dark red,
almost like I was choking.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.530
Like I needed the Heimlech
Maneuver at the restaurant.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.820
And she was like, "It's
cute, I appreciate it.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.460
But you know, I thought this
was just like a friend thing."

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.510
and I was just like,
"Totally is, I'm just dru--"

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.770
Like, you know, when
you're so embarrassed,

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.411
you make up every excuse in the book?

00:04:52.411 --> 00:04:55.530
And I couldn't even come
up with an idea of like,

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.080
"Oh, I was texting about some other girl,"

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.620
because I was literally
sitting in front of her,

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.520
it was in present conversation.

00:05:00.912 --> 00:05:05.912
So we're still friends, we
talk every once in a while.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.990
- [Interviewer] Amazing.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.210
- Hey guys, we're Peralide.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.313
Did you know it's Hispanic Heritage Month?

00:05:23.313 --> 00:05:24.260
- (speaking foreign language)

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.530
- For more Latino content,

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:26.570
- subscribe here.

